| Dice rolled by a script (`XdY` in lib/*.irh) | `INCURSION_FORCE_SCRIPT_DICE=<n>` (`src/VMachine.cpp`). Each die of a roll the script engine evaluates shows `min(n, sides)`; 1 = minimum, 99 = maximum, and script bonuses still add. It does not touch dice that C++ rolls for itself (combat damage, hit points, map generation). Malformed values log one Error and are ignored. |
| Monster hit points | The "Monsters Maximum Hit Points" option (`OPT_MON_MAX_HP`, `src/Values.cpp:2392`) set to any value but NO. It is a character-generation option, so a loaded game takes it from its save, not from the options file: set it in the options file that the fixture's `.char` names on its `options:` line. |
| An item an item generator returns (`Item::GenItem`: gifts, monster gear, floor loot) | `INCURSION_GENITEM_FORCE="name[:plus];name[:plus]"` (`src/Encounter.cpp`). Each GenItem call returns the next entry; with the list used up, generation is unchanged. A probe re-arms it with `GenItemForceArm("...")` and counts uses with `GenItemForceConsumed()` (`inc/Item.h`). Used by tools/check_weapon_types.sh. |
| God-pulse lottery (an INTERVAL god's pulse) | `INCURSION_FORCE_GOD_PULSE=1` or `INCURSION_FORCE_GOD_PULSE=<god name>` (`src/Creature.cpp`, `GodPulsePass`). The 1-in-10 gate always passes. With `1` the pick always chooses the character's patron. With a god's name (for example `Xel`) the pick chooses that god whenever the character is involved with it, patron or not, so a forsaken follower or an apostate gets the pulse through the non-patron pick of real play, due after 5 times the god's interval. The pulse fires when the god's interval is due; the random draws are still taken; an unknown name logs one Error and is ignored. Used by tools/check_force_god_pulse.sh. |
| Percent-chance roll made by a script (`random(n)` in `lib/*.irh`) | `INCURSION_FORCE_SCRIPT_RANDOM=<k>`, k a whole number >= 0. Every `random(n)` a script makes returns `min(k, n-1)`, so k=10 fails a `random(100) >= 50` test and k=90 passes it. `src/VMachine.cpp` (`ScriptRandom`) reads it. A malformed value logs an Error and is ignored. Used by tools/check_force_script_random.sh. |
| Percent-chance roll made in C++ | *none* |
| Rest encounter roll and the monsters a rest adds (`Map::DaysPassed`) | Wizard menu, "Wizard Mode Switches", "Always Rest Safely" set to YES. Rest becomes safe and instant: no encounter roll, no time passes, no new monsters. It also lifts the Goblin Caves depth-1 low-level rest refusal (`lib/dungeon.irh`). Used by tools/check_inherent_lucubration.sh. |
| Spell success roll (the player's percentile spell failure) | Wizard menu, "Wizard Mode Switches", "Ignore Spell Failure" set to YES (`src/Magic.cpp`). Used by tools/check_inherent_lucubration.sh. |
| Door lock roll (Door::Door, both the closed and the secret lock roll) | `INCURSION_DOOR_LOCK_ROLL=<0..99>` (`src/Feature.cpp`). A door locks when the value is below its depth's lock chance. Used by tools/check_door_lock_rate.sh. |
| Lost-sight search roll (Monster::ChooseAction, one turn in three) | `INCURSION_LOSTSIGHT_SEARCH_ROLL=<0..2>` (`src/Monster.cpp`). The value replaces `random(3)`; 0 makes a monster that lost sight of its target search. Unset or any other value leaves the roll unchanged. Used by tools/check_hide_search.sh. |
